"Microsoft Word - Biosecurity Bill 1-09-08 _Paul_.doc (https://assets.ippc.int/static/media/files/reportingobligation/2017/08/11/Cook_Islands_Biosecurity_Act_2008.pdf)\nciteturn2086view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 73; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://assets.ippc.int/static/media/files/reportingobligation/2017/08/11/Cook_Islands_Biosecurity_Act_2008.pdf\",\"lineno\":530}); Total lines: 3054\nL381@P7: “biosecurity specifications” means biosecurity import\nL382@P7: specifications made under section 26 or biosecurity export\nL383@P7: specifications made under section 36;\nL384@P7: \nL385@P7: “biosecurity threat” means the threat of harm being caused or\nL386@P7: adverse effects resulting to animals, plants, human beings, the\nL387@P7: environment or economic activities as a result of the introduction,\nL388@P7-8: establishment or spread of a regulated pest or disease; Biosecurity 9\nL389@P8: “captain”, in relation to an aircraft, means the person for the time\nL390@P8: being in command of the aircraft;\nL391@P8: “Codex Alimentarius Commission” means the international body\nL392@P8: established by the World Health Organization and Food and\nL393@P8: Agriculture Organization to carry out Food Standards Programmes\nL394@P8: for the purpose of protecting the health of consumers and\nL395@P8: facilitating international trade;\nL396@P8: “compliance agreement” means an agreement between the\nL397@P8: Secretary and another person as provided for in section 87;\nL398@P8: “consignment” means a quantity of goods which arrive in the same\nL399@P8: vessel or aircraft and which in accordance with this Act can be\nL400@P8: covered by a single import permit or sanitary or phytosanitary\nL401@P8: certificate;\nL402@P8: “container” means anything in which or by which goods are\nL403@P8: encased, covered, enclosed or packed, including any material in\nL404@P8: contact with the goods, an article of transport equipment, such as a\nL405@P8: lift van moveable tank, sea freight, flat top, roll-on/roll-off\nL406@P8: container, ISO container, or similar structure, either rigid;\nL407@P8: “contamination” means the presence in any item of a pest, not\nL408@P8: constituting an infestation;\nL409@P8: “conveyance” means a ship, aircraft, vehicle or other means of\nL410@P8: transporting people, goods or animals from one location to another,\nL411@P8: while it is being used or prepared for such transport;\nL412@P8: “country of origin” includes a re-exporting country;\nL413@P8: “custodian”, in respect of an item, means the occupier of a place or\nL414@P8: the person in possession and charge of an article, whether lawfully\nL415@P8: or not, but does not include a person who has possession or control\nL416@P8: of the item only for the purpose of taking biosecurity measures in\nL417@P8: respect of it;\nL418@P8: “Director” means the Director of Biosecurity designated under\nL419@P8: section 74, who shall be the person for the time being performing\nL420@P8: the functions of Secretary to the Ministry of Agriculture and, in\nL421@P8: respect of any particular function, a person to whom the function\nL422@P8-9: has been delegated under section 76; 10 Biosecurity\nL423@P9: “disease” means any unhealthy condition in an animal or plant\nL424@P9: which is known or suspected to be caused by an organism, and\nL425@P9: includes a disease transmissible from animals to humans and a\nL426@P9: disease capable of harming the environment;\nL427@P9: “document” means any mode of communicating information in a\nL428@P9: retrievable form, including electronically;\nL429@P9: “environment” includes -\nL430@P9: (a) the ecosystem and its constituent parts, including\nL431@P9: people and communities;\nL432@P9:  (b) all natural and physical resources;\nL433@P9: (c) the qualities and characteristics of locations, places\nL434@P9: and areas.\nL435@P9: “eradication” means the application of measures to eliminate a pest\nL436@P9: or disease from an area;\nL437@P9: “establishment”, in relation to a pest or disease, means the\nL438@P9: perpetuation in an area of the pest or disease for the foreseeable\nL439@P9: future after its entry into the area;\nL440@P9: \nL441@P9: “export” means to take or send goods out of the Cook Islands;\nL442@P9: “exporter” means a person who exports or seeks to export goods,\nL443@P9: other than as the master of the vessel or captain of the aircraft in\nL444@P9: which the goods are carried; and includes a biosecurity clearance\nL445@P9: agent;\nL446@P9: “Fish” means the same as referred to in Section 2 of the Marine\nL447@P9: Resources Act 2005;\nL448@P9: “fittings” means any stall, box, cage, enclosure, pen, net or other\nL449@P9: material used for penning, yarding, confining or containing any\nL450@P9: animal and includes any harness, saddlery, rope, bucket, trough,\nL451@P9: bedding, utensil or implement used in the handling or keeping of\nL452@P9: animals or animal products;\nL453@P9: “fodder” means any water, meat, vegetables, grain or material used\nL454@P9: for the food or litter of animals, or the storage of animal products;\nL455@P9: “garbage” means waste material derived in whole or in part from\nL456@P9: plants, fruit, vegetables, meat or other plant material or animal\nL457@P9: products, or other refuse of any kind that has been associated with any\nL458@P9-10: plants, fruits, vegetables, meat or other plant or animal products; Biosecurity 11\nL459@P10: “genetic material” means any material of plant, animal, microbial\nL460@P10: or other origin containing functional units of heredity;\nL461@P10: “goods” means any kind of moveable property or thing;\nL462@P10: “host material” means any packing material, container, fittings,\nL463@P10: litter, manure, fodder or similar goods that might have had contact\nL464@P10: with animals or plants or their products;\nL465@P10: “import” means to bring goods, or cause goods to be brought, into\nL466@P10: the Cook Islands;\nL467@P10: “importer” means a person who imports or seeks to import goods,\nL468@P10: other than as the master of a vessel or captain of the aircraft in\nL469@P10: which the goods are carried; and includes a biosecurity clearance\nL470@P10: agent;\nL471@P10: “in transit”, in relation to goods, means the goods are not imported\nL472@P10: into an area but pass through it to another area, whether by the\nL473@P10: same or another conveyance, during which time they remain\nL474@P10: enclosed, are not split up, are not combined with other goods, and\nL475@P10: do not have their packaging changed;\nL476@P10: “infected”, in relation to an animal or plant, means that the animal\nL477@P10: or plant is diseased or may have been exposed to the risk of\nL478@P10: infection during the preceding six months;\nL479@P10: “infested”, in relation to an item or area, means that there is present\nL480@P10: in the item or area a living pest or disease;\nL481@P10: “inspection”, in relation to an item, means an official examination\nL482@P10: of the item to determine if any pest or disease is present in the item\nL483@P10: and whether in other respects the item conforms to the\nL484@P10: requirements of this Act;\nL485@P10: “IPPC” means the International Plant Protection Convention of the\nL486@P10: Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations;\nL487@P10: “introduction”, in relation to a pest or disease, means the entry of\nL488@P10: the pest or disease into an area, resulting in its establishment in the\nL489@P10: area;\nL490@P10: “item” means any kind of moveable or immoveable property or\nL491@P10-11: thing, including premises; 12 Biosecurity\nL492@P11: “label”, includes any tag, brand, mark, pictorial or other descriptive\nL493@P11: matter written, printed, stenciled, marked, embossed or impressed\nL494@P11: on, or attached to or included in, belonging to, or accompanying\nL495@P11: any regulated article;\nL496@P11: “living organism” means any organism capable of transferring or\nL497@P11: replicating genetic material, including sterile organisms, viruses,\nL498@P11: viroids, plasmids, bacteriophages and prions;\nL499@P11: “master”, in relation to a vessel, means the person for the time\nL500@P11: being in charge of the vessel, not being the pilot;\nL501@P11: “microbe” means any organism or biotic entity of microscopic\nL502@P11: proportions, whether unicellular, multicellular or sub-cellular in\nL503@P11: common form;\nL504@P11: “Minister” means the Minister of Agriculture;\nL505@P11: “Ministry” means the Ministry of Agriculture;\nL506@P11: “notifiable pest or disease” means a pest or disease which is\nL507@P11: declared under section 67(1) to be notifiable;\nL508@P11: “OIE” means the Organisation Internationale Epizoötique;\nL509@P11: “organism” means a biotic entity capable of reproduction or\nL510@P11: replication [other than a human];\nL511@P11: “packing material” means any fabric, paper, cardboard, plastic,\nL512@P11: wood, straw, grass or leaves used in packing any goods, and any\nL513@P11: other type of material in which goods are covered, enclosed,\nL514@P11: contained or wrapped;\nL515@P11: “pest” means any species, strain or biotype of a plant, animal,\nL516@P11: microbe or pathogenic agent, or any organism, which -\nL517@P11: (a) causes disease; or\nL518@P11: (b) is detrimental to or capable of harming or adversely\nL519@P11: affecting animals or animal products, plants or plant\nL520@P11: products, human beings or the environment;\nL521@P11: “phytosanitary certificate” means a certificate relating to a plant or\nL522@P11: plant product which -\nL523@P11: (a) is issued by the biosecurity authority of the country\nL524@P11-12: of origin or re-exporting country; Biosecurity 13\nL525@P12: (b) certifies that the plant or plant product is\nL526@P12: substantially free from plant pests and diseases and\nL527@P12: in other respects meets the plant health import\nL528@P12: requirements of the receiving country; and\nL529@P12:  (c) is patterned after the model certificates of the IPPC;\nL530@P12: “plant” includes seeds, germplasm, any other part of a plant and a\nL531@P12: dead or preserved plant;\nL532@P12: “plant material” includes any plant, tree, shrub, herb, flower,\nL533@P12: nursery stock, culture, vegetable, tissue culture, or other\nL534@P12: vegetation, and also includes any fruit, seed, spore, and portion or\nL535@P12: product of any plant unless, by any manufacturing process, it has\nL536@P12: been rendered no longer viable, and has been freed from all\nL537@P12: diseases and pests, and has been made incapable of carrying any\nL538@P12: disease or pest;\nL539@P12: “plant product” means –\nL540@P12: (a) plant material;\nL541@P12: (b) timber; and\nL542@P12: (c) any product manufactured wholly or partly from\nL543@P12: one or more plants;\nL544@P12: “PPPO” means the Pacific Plant Protection Organisation;\nL545@P12: “precautionary principle” means the principle that it is not\nL546@P12: unreasonable to refuse permission for an activity that has great\nL547@P12: potential negative impact, even if there is not sufficient scientific\nL548@P12: data to support a refusal, as incorporated in Article 5.7 of the SPS\nL549@P12: Agreement;\nL550@P12: “Premises” means any immoveable property, other than land;\nL551@P12: “Prescribed” means prescribed by this Act or by regulations made\nL552@P12: under it;\nL553@P12: “prohibited import” means a regulated article or the importation or\nL554@P12: ownership of which is prohibited under section 9;\nL555@P12: “re-exporting country”, in relation to any goods, means a country\nL556@P12: which is not the country of origin of the goods, but where a\nL557@P12: container or consignment of goods is opened and re-packed for\nL558@P12: export;\nL559@P12: “receiving country” means a country which is the intended\nL560@P12-13: destination of an article being or proposed to be exported; 14 Biosecurity\nL561@P13: “reconsign”, in relation to a regulated article or consignment which\nL562@P13: has been refused biosecurity import clearance, means to send the\nL563@P13: article or consignment out of the Cook Islands, either by the vessel\nL564@P13: or aircraft on which it was imported or by another vessel or\nL565@P13: aircraft;\nL566@P13:  “regulated article” means –\nL567@P13: (a) any animal or fish product;\nL568@P13: (b) any plant or plant product;\nL569@P13: (c) any living organism, whether modified or not;\nL570@P13: (d) soil, sand, gravel and aggregate;\nL571@P13: (e) any genetic material;\nL572@P13: (f) human remains;\nL573@P13: (g) any host material;\nL574@P13: (h) a regulated pest or disease;\nL575@P13: (i) any clothing, machinery or other article that\nL576@P13: contains or has adhering to it anything mentioned in\nL577@P13: paragraph (a), (b), (c) or (d);\nL578@P13: (j) garbage;\nL579@P13: (k) Any other article, substance, goods or thing\nL580@P13: declared by the Secretary in writing under\nL581@P13: subsection (2) to be a regulated article for the\nL582@P13: purposes of this Act;\nL583@P13: “Regulated consignment” means a consignment of regulated\nL584@P13: articles;\nL585@P13: “regulated pest or disease” means a pest or disease or the\nL586@P13: importation of which into the Cook Islands is prohibited or\nL587@P13: restricted under section 8;\nL588@P13: “regulations” means regulations, orders and any other subsidiary\nL589@P13: legislation made under this Act;\nL590@P13: “sanitary certificate” means an international health certificate\nL591@P13: relating to an animal or animal product which -\nL592@P13: (a) is issued by the biosecurity or agricultural authority\nL593@P13: of the country of origin or re-exporting country;\nL594@P13: (b) certifies that the animal or fish product is\nL595@P13: substantially free from animal pests and diseases\nL596@P13: and in other respects meets the animal health import\nL597@P13: requirements of the receiving country; and\nL598@P13: (c) complies with relevant requirements of the\nL599@P13-14: importing country; Biosecurity 15\nL600@P14: “Secretary” means the Secretary to the Ministry of Agriculture;\nL601@P14: “Service” means the Cook Islands Biosecurity Service constituted\nL602@P14: by section 73;\nL603@P14: “ship’s stores” means any food or other regulated articles carried\nL604@P14: on a vessel or aircraft for consumption or use on the vessel or\nL605@P14: aircraft;\nL606@P14: “specified”, in relation to a requirement, document, procedure or\nL607@P14: any other matter, means specified by the Secretary under section\nL608@P14: 105;\nL609@P14: “spread”, in relation to a pest or disease, means the expansion of\nL610@P14: the geographical distribution of the pest or disease within an area;\nL611@P14: “SPS Agreement” means the World Trade Organisation Agreement\nL612@P14: on the Application of Sanitary and Phytosanitary Measures;\nL613@P14: “status”, in relation to a pest or disease, means its presence,\nL614@P14: absence, prevalence, incidence, distribution and occurrence in an\nL615@P14: area;\nL616@P14: “technical advisory committee” means the head of the department\nL617@P14: or section of government responsible for animal health, plant\nL618@P14: health, fisheries, environment and health quarantine matters\nL619@P14: respectively, not being the Secretary;\nL620@P14: “test” means an examination which goes beyond a visual\nL621@P14: inspection, to determine if a pest or disease is, or is likely to be,\nL622@P14: present or to identify a pest or disease, and includes chemical tests\nL623@P14: of plant material and diagnostic tests in respect of an animal;\nL624@P14: “this Act” includes regulations and orders made under it;\nL625@P14: “timber” includes round wood, sawn wood, wood chips and\nL626@P14: dunnage, with or without bark;\nL627@P14: “treatment” means an authorised procedure for the killing,\nL628@P14: removal, modification or rendering infertile or non-viable of a pest\nL629@P14: or disease by way of cleansing, fumigation, inoculation,\nL630@P14: disinfection, disinfestation, decontamination or otherwise;\nL631@P14: “uncleared”, in relation to a regulated article, means that the article\nL632@P14-15: has not received biosecurity clearance; 16 Biosecurity\nL633@P15: “under official control”, in relation to a pest or disease, means that\nL634@P15: its presence is known, its distribution is limited and its further\nL635@P15: spread is controlled by the exercise of powers under this Act;\nL636@P15: “vehicle” includes a car, truck, bicycle (whether motorized or not),\nL637@P15: a cart and any other wheeled conveyance;\nL638@P15: “vessel” includes a ship, hovercraft, boat, ferry, raft, yacht, canoe\nL639@P15: or pontoon that is used as a conveyance in or on water, whether or\nL640@P15: not it is self-propelled;\nL641@P15: “written” and “in writing” mean any mode of communicating\nL642@P15: information in a retrievable form, including electronically (as to\nL643@P15: which see section 104(2)); and\nL644@P15: “X-Ray machine” means a device to detect regulated articles.\nL645@P15: 3. Application of the Act - (1) This Act applies to every person in the Cook\nL646@P15: Islands, irrespective of the person’s nationality or citizenship.\nL647@P15: (2) This Act applies to all conveyances, containers and goods while they\nL648@P15: are in the Cook Islands, including vessels and aircraft owned or operated by the\nL649@P15: government of a foreign state.\nL650@P15: (3) This Act applies to persons, conveyances, containers and goods outside\nL651@P15: the Cook Islands to the extent needed for its effective enforcement.\nL652@P15: 4. Act binds the State - This Act binds the State, including every Government\nL653@P15: department, statutory authority and statutory corporation, and every person in the\nL654@P15: employment of the Government.\nL655@P15: 5. Responsibility for the Act - (1) The Minister is responsible to the\nL656@P15: Parliament for the implementation of this Act.\nL657@P15: (2) The Secretary is responsible to the Minister for the performance of the\nL658@P15: functions of the Cook Islands Biosecurity Service set out in section 73(2).\nL659@P15: 6. Powers of the Minister - The Minister may –\nL660@P15: (a) give directions in writing to the Secretary concerning\nL661@P15: administrative action needed to implement this Act and to\nL662@P15: achieve the functions of the Service;\nL663@P15: (b) call for reports from the Secretary on any matter pertaining\nL664@P15: to this Act or the functions of the Service;\nL665@P15: (c) by order declare any article, substance, goods or thing to be\nL666@P15: a regulated article for the purposes of this Act; and\nL667@P15: (d) in writing delegate any of the Minister’s functions, powers\nL668@P15: and duties under this Act to the Director a named\nL669@P15: biosecurity officer, other than any legislative or appellate\nL670@P15-16: function or this power to delegate. Biosecurity 17\nL671@P16: 7. Relationship with other Acts - (1) This Act is in addition to and does not\nL672@P16: derogate from any other Act. In particular, but without limiting this rule -\nL673@P16: (a) the requirements relating to imports and exports in Parts 4\nL674@P16: and 5 do not displace any other statutory requirements\nL675@P16: relating to imports and exports, trade in endangered\nL676@P16: species, biosafety, biodiversity or environmental, marine\nL677@P16: laws generally;\nL678@P16: (b) the notification requirements in section 14 relating to\nL679@P16: human health do not displace any other statutory\nL680@P16: requirement relating to such notification;\nL681@P16: (c) the provisions of Part 3 relating to biosecurity port\nL682@P16: quarantine of vessels and aircraft do not displace any other\nL683@P16: provisions relating to quarantine of vessels and aircraft.\nL684@P16: (2) To the extent of any inconsistency between this and any other Act,\nL685@P16: every other Act shall so far as possible be construed so as to fulfill the purpose of this\nL686@P16: Act.\nL687@P16: PART 2\nL688@P16: BIOSECURITY BORDER CONTROL\nL689@P16: 8. Regulated pests and diseases - (1) The Director may by written notice\nL690@P16: declare the pests or diseases –\nL691@P16: (a) the importation of which is prohibited for all purposes;\nL692@P16: (b) the importation of which is permitted subject to conditions\nL693@P16: specified by the Secretary under section 26.\nL694@P16: (2) A person who imports or attempts to import a pest or disease which is\nL695@P16: prohibited under subsection (1)(a) commits an offence.\nL696@P16: (3) A person who imports or attempts to import a pest or disease which is\nL697@P16: regulated under subsection (1)(b) in breach of the conditions of import commits an\nL698@P16: offence.\nL699@P16: (4) When making an order under this section, the Director shall apply pest\nL700@P16: risk analysis, that is to say, the process of evaluating biological or other scientific and\nL701@P16: economic evidence to determine whether a pest or disease should be regulated and the\nL702@P16: nature of any biosecurity measures to be taken against it.\nL703@P16: (5) Before making an order under this section, the Director shall obtain the\nL704@P16: advice of the Secretary and of relevant divisional heads.\nL705@P16: 9. Prohibited imports - (1) The Director may by order prohibit the\nL706@P16: importation of –\nL707@P16: (a) particular regulated articles from all countries; or\nL708@P16: (b) particular regulated articles from one or more particular\nL709@P16: countries of origin,\nL710@P16: (in this Act referred to as “import prohibited articles”) if the importation would present an\nL711@P16: unacceptable biosecurity risk to the Cook Islands.\nL712@P16-17:  (2) An order under this section in respect of an article – 18 Biosecurity\nL713@P17: (a) may be made at any time before biosecurity import\nL714@P17: clearance is granted in respect of the article;\nL715@P17: (b) continues in force until the prohibition is revoked or varied,\nL716@P17: but shall be reviewed every twelve months.\nL717@P17: (3) In making a decision under this section, the Director –\nL718@P17: (a) shall make a biosecurity risk assessment;\nL719@P17: (b) shall have regard to the international obligations of the\nL720@P17: Cook Islands in respect of biosecurity;\nL721@P17:  (c) may apply the precautionary principle.\nL722@P17: (4) Before making an order under this section, the Director shall obtain the\nL723@P17: advice of relevant technical section heads.\nL724@P17: (5) If a person imports or attempts to import a prohibited article –\nL725@P17: (a) the person commits an offence;\nL726@P17: (b) biosecurity import clearance under section 25 will be\nL727@P17: refused for the article.\nL728@P17:  (6) A person who without lawful excuse owns or is in possession of any\nL729@P17: prohibited article commits an offence.\nL730@P17: 10. Biosecurity points of entry and departure - (1) The Director may by notice\nL731@P17: in writing designate as biosecurity points of entry the ports, airports and post offices at\nL732@P17: which regulated articles may enter the Cook Islands.\nL733@P17: (2) Subject to subsection (9), a master or captain who causes or permits an\nL734@P17: incoming vessel or aircraft to berth or land except at a port or airport that is a biosecurity\nL735@P17: point of entry commits an offence.\nL736@P17: (3) A person who imports or attempts to import, a regulated article or\nL737@P17: consignment except at a biosecurity point of entry commits an offence.\nL738@P17: (4) The Director may in writing designate as biosecurity points of\nL739@P17: departure the ports, airports and post offices at which regulated articles can be exported\nL740@P17: and may facilitate a treatment station for the disposal of waste or regulated articles at\nL741@P17: such points.\nL742@P17: (5) A master or captain who causes or permits a vessel or aircraft to leave\nL743@P17: the Cook Islands from a port or airport that is not a biosecurity point of departure\nL744@P17: commits an offence.\nL745@P17: (6) A person who exports or attempts to export, a regulated article or\nL746@P17: consignment except at a biosecurity point of departure commits an offence.\nL747@P17: (7) A designation of a biosecurity point of entry or departure may be\nL748@P17: limited to particular types of vessels, aircraft or articles or to arrivals from or exports to\nL749@P17: particular countries.\nL750@P17:  (8) A post office may only be designated as a biosecurity point of entry or\nL751@P17: departure in respect of regulated articles that at the time of entry or departure are in a mail\nL752@P17: bag or other container that conforms to the requirements of the postal legislation of the\nL753@P17: Cook Islands.\nL754@P17: (9) A vessel or aircraft may berth or land elsewhere than at a biosecurity\nL755@P17: point of entry –\nL756@P17: (a) if constrained by adverse weather, mechanical failure or\nL757@P17-18: superior force; orBiosecurity 19\nL758@P18: (b) if so directed or permitted by the Director or authorized\nL759@P18: biosecurity officer.\nL760@P18: (10) In the circumstances mentioned in subsection (9), the place where the\nL761@P18: vessel has berthed or the aircraft has landed is deemed to be a biosecurity point of entry\nL762@P18: for the purposes of this Act, once the Director has been notified of the berthing or\nL763@P18: landing.\nL764@P18: 11. Designation of biosecurity holding areas - (1) The Director may by notice\nL765@P18: in writing designate –\nL766@P18: (a) any territorial waters or any part of a port as a biosecurity\nL767@P18: port holding area for vessels;\nL768@P18: (b) any part of an airport as a biosecurity port holding area for\nL769@P18: aircraft.\nL770@P18: (2) A biosecurity port holding area is one where incoming conveyances\nL771@P18: may be held for biosecurity inspection pending biosecurity landing clearance or other\nL772@P18: disposition under this Act.\nL773@P18: (3) The Director may by notice in writing designate any area of land at or\nL774@P18: adjacent to a port or airport as a biosecurity goods holding area for incoming or outgoing\nL775@P18: containers and goods.\nL776@P18:  (4) A biosecurity goods holding area is one where incoming or outgoing\nL777@P18: containers or goods may be held for biosecurity inspection pending biosecurity clearance\nL778@P18: or other disposition under this Act.\nL779@P18: (5) The Director may designate any part of a post office that has been\nL780@P18: designated as a biosecurity point of entry or departure as a biosecurity postal holding area\nL781@P18: for incoming or outgoing postal items.\nL782@P18: (6) A biosecurity postal holding area is one where incoming or outgoing\nL783@P18: postal items may be held for biosecurity inspection pending biosecurity clearance or other\nL784@P18: disposition under this Act.\nL785@P18: 12. Management of biosecurity holding areas - (1) Section 40(2) and (3)\nL786@P18: applies to biosecurity holding areas as they apply to biosecurity quarantine stations.\nL787@P18: (2) No person, other than the person in charge of the area or a biosecurity\nL788@P18: officer acting in the course of duty, may enter a biosecurity holding area without the\nL789@P18: written permission of the Director or the permission of the person in charge of the area or\nL790@P18: of a biosecurity officer acting in the course of duty.\nL791@P18: (3) A duly authorised biosecurity officer may, in order to reduce a\nL792@P18: biosecurity threat, lock, and seal or otherwise prevent entry to and exit from a biosecurity\nL793@P18: holding area or any building in it.\nL794@P18: (4) A person who –\nL795@P18: (a) enters a biosecurity holding area without permission\nL796@P18: pursuant to subsection (2); or\nL797@P18: (b) damages, interferes with or in any way reduces the\nL798@P18: effectiveness of measures taken to secure a biosecurity\nL799@P18: holding area, or any regulated article or other item in the\nL800@P18-19: area, 20 Biosecurity\nL801@P19: commits an offence.\nL802@P19: (5) The Director may issue written directions to the person in charge of a\nL803@P19: biosecurity holding area as to the management of the area.\nL804@P19: (6) A person who removes or attempts to remove from a biosecurity\nL805@P19: holding area any regulated article without obtaining biosecurity clearance in respect of it,\nL806@P19: unless for the purpose of biosecurity measures being applied to the article in accordance\nL807@P19: with this Act, commits an offence.\nL808@P19: 13. Biosecurity clearance agents - (1) A person who proposes to import or\nL809@P19: export regulated articles through a port or airport and who will not be present at the\nL810@P19: designated port or airport when biosecurity inspection is to take place shall –\nL811@P19: (a) in writing appoint a person resident in the Cook Islands as\nL812@P19: biosecurity clearance agent for the purposes of this Act; and\nL813@P19: (b) notify the Director in writing of the appointment before the\nL814@P19: agent performs any agency functions.\nL815@P19:  (2) A biosecurity clearance agent appointed under subsection (1) ceases to\nL816@P19: be an agent for the purposes of this Act if the Director notifies the importer or exporter in\nL817@P19: writing that, in the opinion of the Director, the agent’s conduct in the performance of\nL818@P19: functions under this Act renders the agent unacceptable for purposes of this Act.\nL819@P19: (3) Notice under subsection (2) shall be given in sufficient time to allow\nL820@P19: the importer or exporter to appoint another agent.\n"
